Module 5: ADC (AD9234 reference wiring)

Purpose:
- High-speed, 12-bit, 250 MSPS ADC captures differential analog to digital. Provide reference, clock, decoupling and interface to FPGA.

Schematic description (reference):
- ADC: AD9234
  - VIN+ -> ADC_IN_P, VIN- -> ADC_IN_N
  - VREF -> REF_2.5V (use REF5025 or ADR4525 low-noise reference)
  - AVDD, DVDD per datasheet via LDOs and ferrite beads
  - CLOCK_IN: LVDS/LVPECL clock from Si5341 low-jitter source
  - DATA_BUS: 12-bit parallel LVDS/CMOS outputs to FPGA; route with matched pairs
  - SYNC/FRAME pins per device: connect to FPGA lines for alignment

Power and decouple:
- Use recommended decoupling pattern: 0.1uF + 10nF + 1uF at each supply pin; place caps close to pins.

Clocking:
- Low jitter oscillator Si5341 or Si570 generate ADC clock and optionally a phase-aligned clock to FPGA.

Verification:
- With test inputs, measure SNR/ENOB and spectrum using FFT; validate sample clock jitter impact.

Note: Consult the AD9234 datasheet for exact recommended input network and layout guidance.
